# Slide 10 Technical Whitepaper
### Offline-First Edge Orchestration for Partitioned Networks

## Problem
Cloud-centered coordination fails when links degrade. In logistics and field operations, that failure is common and expensive.

## Solution
Slide 10 assumes partition is normal. Nodes adapt operating thresholds, prioritize high-value traffic, protect offline artifacts, and reconcile deterministically when connectivity returns.

## Core mechanisms
1. Adaptive modes (`3f+1`, `2f+1`, `1f+1`)
2. Telemetry-informed mode control
3. Edge filtering
4. Content-addressed integrity
5. Cryptographic signatures
6. Local persistence
7. Reconciliation with reject path

## Security scope
Detects and rejects tampered offline artifacts.  
Does not claim perfect security against full key compromise or formal high-assurance certification requirements.

## Status
Semi-production, testable core suitable for technical evaluation and integration planning.
